const PRIVACY = "Application: TCL Remote Control: Home & TV\nOperator: DEL sisters d.o.o.\n\nThis document describes the applicable conditions for the mobile application and should be read together with the other user-facing legal notice.\n\n## Who We Are\n\nThis Privacy Policy explains how DEL sisters d.o.o. (“we”, “us”, or “our”) handles information when you use TCL Remote Control: Home & TV (the “App”). DEL sisters d.o.o., Lanište 26, 10000 Zagreb, Croatia, is the operator of the App and the primary contact for questions about the processing described here.\n\nWe aim to use only information reasonably needed to provide the App, manage purchases, respond to support requests, and maintain its security. Some App functions operate on your device or local network, while certain optional services require information to be handled by external service providers.\n\n## Information We Process\n\nTelevision connection information. To discover, connect to, and reconnect with a compatible television, the App processes local-network information, including the television’s network address and name. Information about the most recently connected television may be stored on your device to make reconnection easier.\n\nMedia and voice features. When you choose to cast photos or videos, the App accesses the selected media for that purpose. If you use voice controls, the audio needed for the command is sent to your television for processing by that device. These features depend on permissions you grant and on the behavior of the television or associated services.\n\nAI assistant messages. When you use the optional AI assistant, the text of the question you submit is transmitted securely for processing and to generate a response. The App may keep the conversation history on your device. Messages sent for AI assistance are processed through our service infrastructure and a third-party AI provider. The AI service does not need your saved television connection details or local media files to answer your submitted question.\n\nPurchase and subscription information. To administer paid access, restore purchases, and support subscription status, we and our subscription-management service provider process purchase and transaction information and pseudonymous identifiers associated with your device or App installation. These may include an Apple-provided vendor identifier and identifiers created by the subscription service. We may also receive limited App Store campaign attribution information.\n\nSupport correspondence. If you contact us, we receive the information you choose to provide, such as your email address, message, and any details needed to respond. We do not require an account to use the App.\n\nTechnical information. As part of ordinary network communication, limited connection information may be processed temporarily to route requests and protect service availability. We do not operate separate advertising or general-purpose behavioral analytics SDKs in the App, and the App does not collect the advertising identifier for cross-app tracking.\n\n## Why We Process Information\n\nWe process information to enable television discovery and control, deliver user-requested media and voice functions, respond to AI assistant questions, provide and verify purchases, answer support requests, prevent abuse, and comply with applicable legal obligations.\n\nWhere the General Data Protection Regulation applies, our lawful bases may include performance of a contract for core App functionality and paid features; legitimate interests in service security and support, where those interests are not overridden by individual rights; compliance with legal obligations; and consent where required for particular processing activities. Device permissions can be managed through your device settings.\n\n## AI Processing and Service Providers\n\nThe AI assistant is optional. When you submit a question, we send the text of that question to a third-party AI provider through secure service infrastructure in order to return an answer. The service infrastructure we operate for this purpose does not intentionally store AI conversation content or maintain routine message logs. A third-party AI provider may process and retain submitted content according to its applicable privacy and retention practices. We do not represent that such provider-side processing is limited to on-device storage or that a fixed retention period applies.\n\nWe also use service providers that support subscriptions and purchases. They process the identifiers and transaction information required for those functions. Service providers handle information for the relevant service purposes and under their applicable contractual and legal obligations.\n\nPlease avoid sharing passwords, payment information, sensitive personal data, or another person’s private information in your AI questions. You can choose not to use the AI assistant and still use other available App features.\n\n## Sharing of Information\n\nWe disclose information only as reasonably necessary to provide the feature you request, operate purchases and support, comply with valid legal obligations, protect rights and safety, or as otherwise permitted or required by law.\n\nThis includes processing by the third-party AI provider for user-submitted text requests, the subscription-management service for purchase status and associated identifiers, and the App Store payment system for transactions. The television you connect to may separately process content or commands under the device manufacturer’s terms and settings. We do not sell personal information or use the App to serve third-party behavioral advertising.\n\n## International Processing\n\nSome information, including messages submitted to the optional AI assistant, is processed outside the country in which you use the App, including in the United States. Subscription-related service providers may also handle information in other jurisdictions. Privacy and data-protection laws may differ between locations.\n\nWhere applicable law requires additional notices, safeguards, or consent for international processing or disclosure, those requirements must be met before the relevant transfer occurs. You may contact us for more information about the processing relevant to your use of the App.\n\n## Retention and Local Storage\n\nInformation about your most recently connected television and AI chat history may be stored locally on your device for convenience. Such information generally remains until it is overwritten, cleared through available settings, or removed together with the App’s local data. We do not maintain a separate user account containing this history.\n\nOur infrastructure used to relay AI questions does not retain message content or routine request logs. However, information provided to a third-party AI provider may be retained by that provider according to its own practices; we do not have a verified fixed retention period to state here. Subscription and transaction records are retained by relevant service providers for operational, contractual, and legal purposes. Support messages are kept only as long as reasonably necessary to resolve the request and satisfy applicable obligations.\n\n## Your Choices and Rights\n\nYou can control permission-based functions through your device’s privacy settings. You can stop using the AI assistant at any time. You can generally remove locally stored App information by deleting the App and its data; subscription cancellation must be completed separately through your App Store account.\n\nDepending on where you live, you may have rights to request access to, correction or deletion of, or restrictions on the processing of your personal information, as well as rights to object, receive a portable copy, withdraw consent where processing relies on consent, or complain to a competent supervisory authority. These rights may be subject to legal limits and verification requirements.\n\nTo make a privacy request, email lozic@delsisters.store. We will review and respond under applicable law. Because the App does not require an account, we may need enough information to identify the relevant records, and some data may be held independently by third-party providers.\n\n## Security\n\nWe apply reasonable technical and organizational safeguards appropriate to the information involved. Communications with our AI processing infrastructure use encrypted connections. No electronic transmission or storage system can be guaranteed completely secure, and connected televisions and third-party services maintain their own security practices.\n\n## Children and Family Use\n\nThe App is a general television-control utility and does not require the creation of a user account. Parents and guardians should supervise a minor’s use where appropriate, particularly when the minor uses features that transmit information to external services. We do not intentionally request personal information from children for advertising or profiling. Where applicable law requires parental consent or special safeguards, those requirements apply.\n\n## Changes to This Policy\n\nWe may update this Privacy Policy to reflect changes in the App or legal requirements. The revised version will show its updated date and will be made available through the App or its public policy page. Where required, we will provide additional notice or obtain consent before a material change takes effect.\n\n## Contact\n\nDEL sisters d.o.o. | Lanište 26, 10000 Zagreb, Croatia | lozic@delsisters.store";

const TERMS = "Application: TCL Remote Control: Home & TV\nOperator: DEL sisters d.o.o.\n\nThis document describes the applicable conditions for the mobile application and should be read together with the other user-facing legal notice.\n\n## About These Terms\n\nThese Terms of Use (the “Terms”) govern your access to and use of the mobile application TCL Remote Control: Home & TV (the “App”) provided by DEL sisters d.o.o. (“we”, “us”, or “our”). By installing or using the App, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the App.\n\nThe App is intended to provide remote-control and related convenience functions for compatible televisions. Certain features may require a compatible television, access to the same local network, device permissions, or a paid subscription. Availability and performance depend on the device and its software.\n\n## Company and Support\n\nThe App is published and operated by DEL sisters d.o.o., Lanište 26, 10000 Zagreb, Croatia. For questions about these Terms, the App, or purchases, contact lozic@delsisters.store.\n\n## Eligibility and Appropriate Use\n\nYou may use the App only in accordance with applicable laws and the rights of other people. If you are under the age at which you may legally agree to these Terms in your jurisdiction, a parent or legal guardian must authorize or supervise your use where required by law.\n\nYou may use the App only with televisions, accounts, networks, and content that you own or are authorized to control. You must not attempt to interfere with other people’s devices, bypass access controls, disrupt network services, or use the App for unlawful purposes.\n\n## License to Use the App\n\nSubject to these Terms and the applicable App Store usage rules, we grant you a limited, personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to use the App on devices that you own or control. The App is licensed, not sold.\n\nYou may not copy, redistribute, sell, sublicense, or modify the App; attempt to obtain its source code; or circumvent technical restrictions, except where expressly permitted by mandatory law or applicable open-source licenses. We reserve all rights not expressly granted.\n\n## Television Control and Media Features\n\nDepending on the television model and supported functions, the App may offer power, volume and playback controls, navigation, text entry, application shortcuts, voice-control functions, and the selection of photos or videos for display on a television.\n\nThe App uses your device’s permitted local-network and media capabilities to provide these functions. You remain responsible for the devices and media you choose to connect, control, or display. Television manufacturers and connected services may apply their own terms and privacy practices to activity occurring on the television.\n\nWe do not guarantee compatibility with every television, firmware version, application, network configuration, or feature. Some functions may require additional permissions or may become unavailable following changes outside our control.\n\n## AI Assistance\n\nThe App may include an optional AI assistant designed to provide general information and troubleshooting guidance about television setup, connection, and related use. When you choose to submit a question, the text you provide is processed through our service infrastructure and a third-party AI provider so that an answer can be returned.\n\nAI-generated answers may be incomplete, outdated, or incorrect. They are informational suggestions, not official manufacturer instructions or a guarantee of any result. Check important instructions against your television’s documentation and exercise judgment before changing settings or following troubleshooting steps.\n\nDo not enter passwords, payment card details, sensitive personal information, or confidential information in the AI assistant. You must not use the AI assistant to request or produce unlawful, harmful, or infringing material. We may limit an AI feature where reasonably necessary to protect users, comply with law, or maintain service integrity.\n\n## Subscriptions and In-App Purchases\n\nThe App may offer paid features through in-app purchases or automatically renewing subscriptions. The specific features, price, billing interval, any free-trial period, and other commercial terms are displayed in the App before you confirm a purchase. You are charged through the payment account associated with the Apple App Store.\n\nUnless canceled before renewal in accordance with Apple’s applicable procedures, an automatically renewing subscription continues for successive billing periods and the applicable subscription fee will be charged. You can manage or cancel subscriptions through your device’s Apple account subscription settings. Deleting the App does not cancel an active subscription.\n\nIf a free trial is offered, it is subject to the conditions shown at sign-up. You may lose any unused portion of an introductory offer when you purchase a subscription, to the extent permitted by applicable rules. Where available, you may restore eligible purchases using the App’s restore-purchases function.\n\nPayment processing, cancellation, billing disputes, and refund eligibility are governed by the applicable App Store rules and mandatory consumer protection law. Nothing in these Terms limits any non-waivable statutory rights.\n\n## Intellectual Property and TCL Trademark Authorization\n\nThe App’s independently developed software, interface, and original content are owned by us or our licensors and are protected by applicable intellectual property laws.\n\nTCL and related marks belong to their respective rights holders. Use of the TCL name and authorized brand elements in connection with the App is made pursuant to a trademark authorization agreement with the relevant rights holder. This authorization does not transfer trademark ownership to us or to users.\n\nThe App is published, operated, billed, and supported by DEL sisters d.o.o. The trademark authorization should not be interpreted as making the trademark owner responsible for the App’s operation, subscriptions, customer support, or data handling. No rights to use third-party trademarks are granted to you under these Terms.\n\n## Third-Party Devices and Services\n\nThe App may interact with devices and services supplied by third parties, including television operating systems, installed TV applications, the App Store, and service providers necessary to deliver optional features. Those products and services are outside our direct control and may be subject to separate terms and policies.\n\nWe are not responsible for interruptions or changes made by third-party devices or services, except to the extent responsibility cannot lawfully be excluded.\n\n## Availability, Changes, and Termination\n\nWe may update, improve, suspend, or discontinue features for technical, legal, security, or operational reasons. Feature availability may vary by jurisdiction, television, device, or network conditions. Where required by law, we will provide appropriate notice of material changes.\n\nWe may restrict access where necessary because of misuse, security concerns, or a legal obligation. You may stop using the App at any time by uninstalling it, but you must separately cancel any active subscription.\n\n## Disclaimers and Liability\n\nTo the extent permitted by applicable law, the App is provided on an “as available” basis without a guarantee of uninterrupted operation, universal compatibility, or error-free AI responses. We use reasonable care in operating the App but cannot control all television hardware, networks, and third-party services.\n\nNothing in these Terms excludes or limits liability for fraud, intentional misconduct, personal injury caused by negligence where prohibited, or any other liability or consumer right that cannot lawfully be excluded. Subject to those protections, we are not liable for indirect or consequential losses that were not reasonably foreseeable when these Terms were agreed.\n\n## Governing Law and Consumer Rights\n\nThese Terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Croatia, without depriving consumers of mandatory protections that apply under the laws of their country of habitual residence. Disputes are subject to the competent courts determined under applicable law. Nothing in this section restricts rights to bring claims before a court or authority where mandatory law permits.\n\n## Changes to These Terms\n\nWe may revise these Terms to reflect changes in the App, applicable law, or our practices. The updated version will state its revision date and will be made available through the App or associated public pages. If a change materially affects your rights, we will provide additional notice or request agreement where required.\n\n## Contact\n\nDEL sisters d.o.o. | Lanište 26, 10000 Zagreb, Croatia | lozic@delsisters.store";

